  "steps": [
    "A request or file leaves the bank from inside its own perimeter.",
    "It crosses one of three channels: an API call with an API key or OAuth token, a signed webhook from us, or an encrypted file drop.",
    "At our perimeter every channel is encrypted in transit and checked: keys, allow-lists, rate limits and malware scans. Only allowed calls reach the platform.",
    "When something changes, we call the bank's webhook: the body is signed and timestamped, delivered with retries, and checked by the bank.",
    "A trusted third party is optional: a broker or hub that relays messages, a certificate authority, an identity provider, or a clean room so neither side sees raw personal data.",
    "Both sides log every call, keep keys apart per bank, and rotate them on a schedule."
  ]
